/**
 * Shared log tag for every diagnostic call from the app, so an
 * operator can `adb logcat -s ConvoScribe` and see the whole app
 * narrative in one stream regardless of which sub-package emitted
 * the line.
 *
 * The tag is `ConvoScribe` (the application id / display name). The
 * native side keeps its own tag (`sherpa-onnx`) for engine library
 * errors and is filtered separately with
 * `adb logcat -s sherpa-onnx`.
 *
 * The object also exposes thin wrappers around [Log.w] and [Log.i]
 * so call sites read `Log.w(...)` rather than
 * `android.util.Log.w(TAG, ...)` and cannot forget to thread the
 * tag through. The wrappers take a vararg of [Any] formatted with
 * [toString]; production code uses them sparingly for high-value
 * events (recording start / stop, diarization summary, model
 * download completed) so a noisy device log does not blow up.
 */
